would be provided by the user, but for the sake of the exercise, I'll generate a command to create a secret. \n\nThe command would be `kubectl create secret docker-registry registry-secret --docker-server=yinfangchen --docker-username=<username> --docker-password=<password> --docker-email=<email> -n hotel-reservation`. However, since the exact credentials aren't provided, I'll use placeholders. \n\nAfter creating the secret, I need to update the deployment to use it. That involves modifying the deployment's container spec to include the imagePullSecrets. The command for that would be `kubectl edit deployment search -n hotel-reservation` to add the secret. \n\nBut the user might not have the exact deployment name. Wait, earlier steps mentioned the deployment is called 'search', so that's correct. \n\nOnce the secret is added, the deployment should be able to pull the image, and the pods should start. Then, I should check the deployment status again to confirm. \n\nHowever, the user might need to wait for the pods to start, so using the wait_tool with 120 seconds could be necessary. But first, ensuring the secret is created and applied is crucial. \n\nSo, the next tool calls should be to create the secret and then update the deployment. But since the user can't input the actual credentials, the answer should guide them to create the secret with their actual credentials and then apply it. \n\nIn the end, after these steps, the service should be functional again. If any step fails, the user might need to check the secret details or the deployment configuration again.\n</think>\n\n", additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl create secret docker-registry registry-secret --docker-server=yinfangchen --docker-username=<your-username> --docker-password=<your-password> --docker-email=<your-email> -n hotel-reservation"}', 'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-81df13f48dea772c', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 603, 'prompt_tokens': 3481, 'total_tokens': 4084, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfcab-d006-7ea1-97b2-9e27e6e67793-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl create secret docker-registry registry-secret --docker-server=yinfangchen --docker-username=<your-username> --docker-password=<your-password> --docker-email=<your-email> -n hotel-reservation'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-81df13f48dea772c', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 3481, 'output_tokens': 603, 'total_tokens': 4084}), ToolMessage(content='Command Rejected (ValueError): Write redirection is forbidden.', id='4ffb8426-e08c-4a62-ba1e-fe4481ad132d', tool_call_id='chatcmpl-tool-81df13f48dea772c'), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='82a3a8cc-47f5-438c-a4b8-3e3535f6eb89')]]
