d, perhaps they need to retrieve it from a secure source or use a different method. But given the tools available, the best approach is to execute the `kubectl create secret` command with the required parameters, ensuring that the secret is properly created in the namespace. This will allow the deployment to pull the image, thereby resolving the pod creation issue.\n</think>\n\ntool name: exec_kubectl_cmd_safely\nreasoning: The absence of secrets in the `hotel-reservation` namespace confirms the root cause: the deployment cannot pull the private registry image `yinfangchen/hotelreservation:latest` due to missing credentials. We must create a `docker-registry` secret with valid credentials for the private registry to enable image pulling.\n\ntool_call: {"command": "kubectl create secret docker-registry registry-secret --docker-server=yinfangchen --docker-username=<your-username> --docker-password=<your-password> --docker-email=<your-email> -n hotel-reservation"}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=456, prompt_tokens=2760, total_tokens=3216, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfcac-2492-7ae1-8dbe-2735a2b58b20-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 2760, 'output_tokens': 456, 'total_tokens': 3216}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='fc98b283-1ead-47a2-8e9f-d7a906f85de0')]]
